# Pipfile
# According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
# However, in case of collaboration, if having platform-specific dependencies or dependencies
# having no cross-platform support, pipenv may work locally, but fail at packaging time or when
# installing on other machines. (Maybe *nix only packages, etc...)
# Nevertheless, if there is only one platform targetted, you can commit it but it is a trade-off.
# With that in mind, it is recommended to really use only one .python-version and a pipenv with
# --python flag in the Pipfile.lock (michelangelo17/Pipenv -r pipenv#437)
# Pipfile.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, this is for now a project-specific cache.
pdm.lock

# PEP 582; used by e.g. github.com/David-OConnor/pyflow and github.com/pdm-project/pdm
